// SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
/**
 * Inline technology marks for the docs pages - the `<!--l:key-->` markdown marker.
 *
 * A build page that names Helm, Kubernetes, k3s, nginx, Rust or a distro, and the
 * Shoulders of giants page that credits the projects Lolly is built from, are naming
 * things the reader already recognises by their marks, and a mark next to the word
 * is faster to scan than the word alone. These ship INLINE in the HTML (not as
 * <img>) for one reason: an inline <svg> inherits `currentColor`, so a mark takes
 * the colour of the text it sits in - in both themes, with no second asset and no
 * per-mark colour rule. Sizing is CSS's (`.doc-logo` in docs/build.ts); the markup
 * here carries no width/height at all.
 *
 * Source: simple-icons (https://github.com/simple-icons/simple-icons), whose icon
 * files are CC0-1.0. Each is already a single 24×24 path, taken VERBATIM - the
 * only changes are dropping the <title> (the marks are decorative here, the word
 * beside them is the accessible name) and stating `fill="currentColor"` +
 * `aria-hidden="true"` on the root. A trademark is not ours to redraw, so a mark
 * we cannot obtain cleanly is simply not shown:
 *
 *  - RKE2 - simple-icons has none, and the official artwork (rancher/rke2-docs
 *    static/img/logo-stacked-*.svg) is a multi-element lockup WITH the wordmark at
 *    138×171. Reducing that to a 24×24 glyph would be redrawing someone's mark, so
 *    RKE2 is named in prose without one.
 *  - Open Build Service - same outcome: openSUSE/artwork carries only the sticker
 *    art, and open-build-service's own obs-logo_small.svg is a coloured lockup with
 *    live <text>. Named without a mark.
 *
 * Every mark here is used editorially - to refer to the thing it stands for. The
 * marks belong to their owners.
 *
 * Keys are the plain technology name (`node`, not `nodedotjs`); the comment on each
 * entry records the simple-icons file it came from, so a refresh is a re-fetch of a
 * known path rather than a hunt.
 */
